  <section id="faq" class="lab-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Sales training FAQ</div>
      <h2>Questions buyers ask about B2B sales training and coaching.</h2>
      <div class="faq-list lab-faq-list">
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What is B2B sales training?</h3><p>B2B sales training develops the skills sellers need to prospect, open conversations, ask useful questions, communicate value, handle objections, qualify opportunities, follow up, and move business buyers toward a clear next step. Strong programs connect learning to the company’s offer, buyers, sales process, and real selling situations.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What is Sales Execution Lab?</h3><p>Sales Execution Lab is CallTeam’s practical B2B sales training and coaching service. It uses real sales evidence, targeted coaching, live practice, AI-assisted analysis where appropriate, and field application to improve the conversations and behaviors buyers experience.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Who is Sales Execution Lab for?</h3><p>Sales Execution Lab is built for founders, SDRs, BDRs, account executives, full-cycle sellers, sales managers, and B2B teams that need sharper prospecting, discovery, objection handling, qualification, follow-up, and pipeline execution.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Is Sales Execution Lab customized to our company?</h3><p>Yes. The coaching is built around the company’s offer, buyers, sales roles, calls, messages, objections, follow-up, pipeline stages, and active opportunities. The goal is to improve the selling situations the team actually faces rather than deliver a generic course.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Does the program include cold calling training?</h3><p>Yes. Cold calling and outbound sales training can cover call preparation, relevant openings, tone, pacing, questions, listening, resistance, qualification, voicemail, follow-up, and securing the next step. The work can use real calls and live practice rather than scripts alone.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can you train SDRs and BDRs?</h3><p>Yes. SDR and BDR training can focus on prospecting discipline, cold calls, email and LinkedIn messages, opening relevance, objection handling, qualification, meeting quality, follow-up, and clean handoff notes.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can you coach account executives and full-cycle sellers?</h3><p>Yes. AE and full-cycle seller coaching can focus on discovery, value communication, qualification, multi-stakeholder conversations, follow-up, deal movement, proposals, negotiation behavior, and maintaining a clear next step.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Do you provide founder sales coaching?</h3><p>Yes. Founder sales coaching helps founders translate deep product knowledge into a clearer buyer conversation, ask better questions, avoid over-explaining, handle resistance, qualify fit, and move opportunities forward with more control.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Does Sales Execution Lab use AI sales coaching or AI role-play?</h3><p>AI-assisted tools can support call transcription, pattern analysis, role-play, objection simulations, practice, scorecards, and feedback organization where appropriate. Experienced human coaches interpret the context, buyer psychology, tone, commercial relevance, and behavior that needs to change.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What is the difference between sales training and sales coaching?</h3><p>Sales training teaches a skill, framework, or shared standard. Sales coaching helps a seller apply that standard to current behavior, calls, messages, and opportunities. Sales Execution Lab connects both: teams learn what good looks like, practice it, apply it, review the evidence, and improve again.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>What is the difference between sales enablement and sales training?</h3><p>Sales enablement is the broader system of content, tools, process, onboarding, training, and support that helps sellers perform. Sales training develops specific knowledge and skills. Sales Execution Lab focuses on the execution layer: what sellers say, do, ask, hear, write, and move forward.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can virtual sales training work for a remote team?</h3><p>Yes. Virtual sales training can be highly practical when it includes real examples, live practice, call review, role-specific feedback, manager reinforcement, and field application between sessions. Remote delivery also makes it easier to coach distributed teams consistently.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>How do you measure sales coaching improvement?</h3><p>Measurement can include execution scorecards, conversation quality, relevant questions, objection exploration, clear next steps, meeting acceptance, follow-up completion, opportunity movement, stage conversion, and consistency across sellers. The exact measures depend on the role and sales motion.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>How long does B2B sales coaching take?</h3><p>The right duration depends on the team, skill gaps, sales cycle, roles, and amount of reinforcement required. A focused workshop can address a narrow issue, while lasting behavior change usually requires diagnosis, practice, field application, review, and repeated coaching.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Can the Lab review our current calls, scripts, and follow-up?</h3><p>Yes. Relevant inputs can include call recordings or transcripts, talk tracks, emails, LinkedIn messages, objection notes, CRM entries, discovery notes, stalled opportunities, qualification standards, and follow-up sequences.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>Does Sales Execution Lab replace done-for-you outbound?</h3><p>No. Sales Execution Lab improves how your people sell. CallTeam’s done-for-you services help execute calling, lead follow-up, qualification, and appointment setting. A company may need one or both depending on whether the gap is internal capability, execution capacity, or both.</p></article>
        <article class="faq-item"><h3>How is Sales Execution Lab different from the 90-Day Revenue Engine?</h3><p>Sales Execution Lab is the people-performance offer. It improves calls, messages, discovery, objections, qualification, follow-up, and deal behavior. The 90-Day Revenue Engine addresses the wider sales system, including ICP, list process, tools, CRM workflow, reporting, and revenue rhythm.</p></article>
